        "title": "Hindu pilgrimage",
        "text": "This a must place to visit, most Hindus come to Nepal to visit temple. Again we visited this time on Monday, generally Monday's are busy but being a holy day it was very busy. Here there are different type of Darsan, if you want close darsan there is a long queue to join it could take hours on busy day. There is an another queue which shorter still able to see from climbing a ramp this is in between the Nandi ( the bull) and the temple. There are 4 doors for Darsan only one door opens in the morning but in afternoon pilgrims can see from all 4 doors. Other way of avoiding the long queue is doing puja with local priest, they have their own ways.",
